  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-09T16:29:10.846Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "On the VRChat public Discord, there’s been collaboration between me and a few other users around the topic of bettering the servers and reducing lag. It’s my understanding that VRChat is not hosted on dedicated servers and are outsourced to a hosting company. This has caused many problems with stability and performance. And it doesn’t help that there’s been a huge spike in playercount. (Which leads to my proposal)\n\nSolution: Get a more premium host or host the game on dedicated hardware.\nCaveat: How to afford improvements on a free game?\n\nSolution: Implement in-game banners and advertising on the hub worlds and optional on player worlds (in exchange for say, a bigger world limit) \n\nI think this solution would actually create a more immersive world as long as they don’t have audio and unintrsive and in turn, we can further allow the expansion of VRChat to become something bigger!\n\nThanks to everyone’s suggestions on the Discord.\n\n\nThank you for your time.\n\n-Pri",
